  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Recipients may use a supervised holding area for up to twenty minutes; every held item needs its recipient’s name and collection deadline.\", \"decision\": \"How should claimed items be held while recipients continue browsing?\", \"goal\": \"Help usable household goods reach interested neighbors while keeping contributions, claims, and final collection understandable.\", \"problem\": \"Neighbors are organizing a one-day fair for clean, usable household goods that people no longer need. Giving and taking are both optional, and no payment or matching contribution is required. Volunteers have intake space, category tables, reserve shelves, a holding area, carts, and simple item records. Contributors choose in advance whether unclaimed goods should be returned during the closing collection period or donated through an arranged pickup.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nRecipients bring claimed items to the holding volunteer, who records their names and deadlines before placing the goods on shelves. A single handover establishes responsibility and makes the promised collection time clear to both people.\nTable volunteers prepare holding tags for claimed items and send them with a runner to the supervised holding area. Recipients can keep browsing while the tagged transfer preserves their identity and collection deadline through the handover.\nRecipients complete holding tags with their names and deadlines, and the volunteer checks the tags before storing the items. The claimant supplies the details directly while the volunteer confirms that every stored item has a usable collection record."
    }
  ],
